                    sum_r5_none:            `No contracts secured at the Summit.`,

                    insight_escaped:        `Commodity trap escaped: across five cycles you co-sequenced quality, certification, market and brand — hedged through the price collapse, funded a reserve, built traceability before the EUDR bit, and matched every capability to a buyer who would pay for it. Premium revenue cleared 60%, the cup is solidly specialty, members stayed, and all three buyers signed. COCACAP now captures value it used to hand to traders and roasters.`,
                    insight_trapped:        `Still in the commodity trap: the transformation didn't fully land. One or more dimensions — quality, certification, market or resilience — didn't reinforce the others, so the cooperative remains substantially a price-taker selling at a differential to the ICE C price.`,
                    insight_budget:         `Budget exhaustion: spending the entire Year-1 budget left no buffer, and the price collapse hit member payments with nothing in reserve to absorb it. Ambition outran resilience.`,
                    insight_hedge:          `Unmanaged price risk: hitting the 22% collapse unhedged converted a market move into a financial crisis, draining the capital that the quality and certification strategy depended on. Hedging is what lets a cooperative execute a multi-year plan.`,
                    insight_stranded:       `Stranded certifications: you paid for certs without the buyer relationships to monetise them. A certification only captures a premium when a buyer specifically demands it — capability and market must be built together.`,
                    insight_shipment:       `Quality–market mismatch: you secured a specialty buyer before the cup score could satisfy them, and the first shipment failed. A buyer relationship without the quality behind it damages the relationship and the booked premium alike.`,
                    insight_eudr:           `EUDR failure: treating traceability as overhead cost you your biggest buyer when the EU Deforestation Regulation made plot-level data a condition of market access. Distant regulation became an existential supply-chain requirement.`,
                    insight_brand:          `Brand erosion: a DTC brand built on inconsistent quality — and uniform member pricing that let free-riding persist — destroyed the equity you were spending to create. Quality systems must precede brand communication.`,
                    insight_summit:         `Buyer Summit swept: Nordic Brews, Tablón de Cacao and Cooperativa Justa all signed — a diversified premium portfolio across specialty coffee, fine-flavor cacao and certified supply, earning the 1.15× bonus.`,
                    insight_nosummit:       `The Buyer Summit yielded no signed contract: the buyers couldn't verify that COCACAP can deliver their requirements consistently. Market access without proven capability is no access at all.`,
                    insight_quality:        `The cup never reached specialty grade (80+): without consistent quality, every downstream move — certification, brand, specialty buyers — rests on a foundation that isn't there.`,

                    hint_budget:            `You blew the Year-1 budget — there's no buffer for the price collapse. Stabilize finances and rebuild a reserve before pursuing more ambition.`,
                    hint_hedge:             `The unhedged collapse gutted your finances. Build a stabilization fund and use multi-year forward contracts so the next price shock can't repeat this.`,
                    hint_nohedge:           `You left the Year-2 crop unhedged. A collapse is coming — every later round is harder if it lands on an unhedged balance sheet.`,
                    hint_quality:           `No Q-grader yet — you can't prove or improve cup quality. Build the cupping feedback loop before chasing specialty buyers.`,
                    hint_trace:             `Still no plot-level traceability. The EU Deforestation Regulation will make it a condition of market access — invest before you lose your biggest buyer.`,
                    hint_shipment:          `The first specialty shipment failed because the quality wasn't there yet. Quality has to lead the buyer relationship, never trail it.`,
                    hint_eudr:              `You lost your biggest buyer to EUDR enforcement. Traceability is strategy, not paperwork.`,
